1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,607
Voluntary carbon markets face an existential trust problem.

2
00:00:04,557 --> 00:00:15,976
Today, credit verification relies on static, disconnected PDF audit reports that take months to review, invite double-counting, and obscure baseline calculations.

3
00:00:15,976 --> 00:00:22,161
CarbonProof AI introduces a zero-trust, deterministic verification platform.

4
00:00:22,161 --> 00:00:32,565
We bridge physical evidence documents, explainable automated risk scoring, strict separation of audit duties, and dual-layer blockchain reconciliation.

5
00:00:32,565 --> 00:00:45,104
Here in the Project Explorer, every environmental initiative is cataloged with structured metadata: methodology standards, crediting periods, geographic coordinates, and registry references.

6
00:00:45,104 --> 00:00:55,299
Rather than accepting high-level claims, CarbonProof AI treats every carbon credit assertion as an unverified hypothesis until backed by immutable evidence.

7
00:00:55,299 --> 00:01:09,700
Under the Evidence Vault, raw documentation—remote sensing GeoTIFFs, ground biomass sensor logs, and baseline additionality spreadsheets—are cryptographically fingerprinted using SHA-256.

8
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:20,807
Notice our critical ethical distinction: matching cryptographic fingerprints proves byte-for-byte immutability, ensuring documents cannot be retroactively altered after submission.

9
00:01:20,807 --> 00:01:27,825
It establishes verifiable custody without making false claims of replacing on-ground physical inspection.

10
00:01:27,825 --> 00:01:35,377
Next, our deterministic rules engine evaluates submitted projects against standardized carbon accounting criteria.

11
00:01:35,377 --> 00:01:42,278
Unlike black-box neural networks, CarbonProof's scoring is completely transparent and reproducible.

12
00:01:42,278 --> 00:01:51,432
Reviewers see the exact rule IDs evaluated, severity ratings from Low to Critical, and actionable remediation recommendations.

13
00:01:51,432 --> 00:01:57,044
An auditor knows precisely why a score was assigned and what adjustments are required.

14
00:01:57,044 --> 00:01:59,895
Integrity requires governance.

15
00:01:59,895 --> 00:02:08,515
Our platform enforces strict separation of duties: project developers are prohibited from reviewing or approving their own submissions.

16
00:02:08,515 --> 00:02:18,697
Accredited reviewers inspect findings, review evidence integrity, and record binding audit decisions accompanied by cryptographically signed justifications.

17
00:02:18,697 --> 00:02:28,398
Once approved, credit batches are minted with mandatory UUID idempotency keys to eliminate double-issuance risks across network retries.

18
00:02:28,398 --> 00:02:37,643
When credits are retired, an on-chain event burns the tokens on our Solidity registry contract while recording a unique retirement serial certificate.

19
00:02:37,643 --> 00:02:47,851
A background reconciliation worker continuously polls the EVM node, resolving divergences and ensuring off-chain ledgers mirror on-chain finality.

20
00:02:47,851 --> 00:02:59,882
Finally, any market participant, corporate buyer, or regulator can verify project legitimacy through our unauthenticated public portal using a project UUID or evidence hash.

21
00:02:59,882 --> 00:03:08,632
CarbonProof AI delivers transparency without greenwashing, providing the cryptographic rigor voluntary carbon markets urgently need.

